{"availability":"available","full":"SarthakBharad/coursera-notes","name":"coursera-notes","description":"My Coursera study notes as a static Next.js + TypeScript site: course roadmaps, a focused reader with search, callouts, hidden answers, progress tracking and dark mode. Notes are plain Markdown.","category":"Education","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-10T17:45:29Z","updated":"2026-10-10T18:11:31Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://coursera-notes.vercel.app","topics":["coursera","dark-mode","data-structures-and-algorithms","google-it-support","learning-notes","markdown","nextjs","nextjs-app-router","notes","pnpm","react","static-site","study-notes","typescript","vercel"],"demo":"https://coursera-notes.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:53.213Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:53.213Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:53.213Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T07:59:53.213Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["My Coursera study notes, turned into a fast, searchable reading site.","A static website for reading the notes I write while working through Coursera programs. The home page lists every program I'm taking, each program page shows its full course roadmap, and every module of notes gets its own focused reading page.","Notes are plain Markdown files in content/. They're turned into HTML at build time, so the finished site is just static files with no server and no database. Visits are counted with Vercel Web Analytics, which uses no cookies and only records anonymous page views."],"features":["Program picker on the home page, with filters, a course track per program and reading progress","Course roadmap for each program, listing every course and module, including ones without notes yet","Sticky \"On this page\" list that follows your scroll, a reading progress bar and estimated time left","Callo